+## 4. NEW finding — lockfile reproducibility gap (P2)
+
+With `poetry.lock` still absent from main, every deploy builds via the `poetry lock --no-interaction` fallback, i.e. **dependencies are re-resolved at build time**. Consequences: (a) two deploys of the same commit can produce different dependency sets; (b) an upstream PyPI release can silently change a production image; (c) build-time resolution adds latency and a third-party availability dependency to every deploy. Once the deploy plane is unblocked, the first successful deploys will bake in whatever upstream state exists at that moment — unpinned.
+
